WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.680
'The men holding Bratton
used this boy as a suicide bomber.'

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.240
It's him. isn't it?
It looks like him.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.560
He owes me a debt of honour.

4
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.600
'I demand the release of my brother.
Mohammed Jassim Ali.'

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.520
'Unless this holy warrior is freed.
the hostage will be executed.'

6
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.560
'Tell Porter he's been reactivated.'

7
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.040
"Porter's gone AWOL. sir." Have you
any idea where he might be headed?

8
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.320
"The tracker in his tooth
has him 35 clicks east of here."

9
00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.200
"30 degrees. 30.24 minutes north.
47 degrees. 49 point..."

10
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.000
..at a safe house in an
apartment block in Basra City.

11
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.120
Go. go. go!

12
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.000
"It's a southern suburb of Basra -"
Yes!

13
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.480
I know it. Porter's chasing
the only lead he has.

14
00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.720
He's outside the safe house that
was used to hold Kenneth Bratton.

15
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.320
Do you want me to contact Basra
police. have them intercept Porter?

16
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.000
No.

17
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.720
He's waited seven years for
a second chance. Let him have it.

18
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.600
'Shoot him! John. shoot him!'

19
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.000
It's OK.

20
00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.040
Hakim Al Nazeri.

21
00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.200
Hakim Al Nazeri!

22
00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.360
Hakim Al Nazeri.

23
00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.160
Hakim Al Nazeri.

24
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.560
Hakim Al Nazeri.

25
00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.280
We're both gonna have a much easier
time if you can speak English.

26
00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.400
I speak English.
Good.

27
00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.640
Where is Hakim Al Nazeri?
I don't know what you're talk...

28
00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.560
Aaaargh! Aieee!

29
00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.240
Alright. Let's try that again.
shall we?

30
00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.800
Point one. our friends there came
running after hearing his name.

31
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.400
Point two. before the invasion this
place was a safe house for a hostage.

32
00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.080
I know that.
I was sent to get him out.

33
00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:02.200
Point three. I'm gonna start using
this knife in more inventive ways

34
00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.960
unless you tell me where
they're holding

35
00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.920
the remaining 95 percent
of the English infidel.

36
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.920
They will kill you. my friend.
Maybe.

37
00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.600
Or maybe they'll hear what I've got
to trade.

38
00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.200
You need to ask yourself how much
Hakim wants Jassim out of Belmarsh.

39
00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.080
Who is this?
Do you miss me?

40
00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.280
"Porter!"
I contacted Sword of Islam.

41
00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.080
I'm off to rendezvous
with my pet theory. Hakim?

42
00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.280
Could be a trap.
could be a wild goose chase.

43
00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.040
I'm gonna have to hang up now.
Porter. keep this line open.

44
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.160
Porter?! Shit!

45
00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.800
So. now we can't be traced. OK?

46
00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.720
Take the next left.

47
00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.480
What are you doing?
Call of nature.

48
00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.400
This road better be flat.

49
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.360
Is this it?
You'll soon find out.

50
00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.080
Out!

51
00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.960
Aaargh! It hurts!

52
00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.760
We really can't go on like this.

53
00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.320
All yours. hero.

54
00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:51.480
Who are you? I'm sorry. sir.
I can't answer that question.

55
00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:12.560
We've just lost Porter.
We've lost him. too. Shit!

56
00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:15.880
We lost contact with Bravo team
at 15:21 GMT. 18:21 local time.

57
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:21.040
In our last communication he claimed
to be heading to a rendezvous

58
00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.840
with a former Mukhabarat colonel.
Hakim Al Nazeri.

59
00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:28.120
a man we believe might be the
commander of Sword of Islam.

60
00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.680
This satellite image of Al Kanan
was Porter's last known position.

61
00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:35.680
It was taken at 18:36 local time

62
00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:39.680
and shows four vehicles outside the
building. Track the vehicles?

63
00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:44.080
No. By the time we got a second
satellite image an hour ago.

64
00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:48.200
the vehicles were gone. And Porter.
We have Charlie team on standby.

65
00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:51.160
We can have then on the ground
in Basra in five hours.

66
00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:55.080
And a helicopter to where they might
find clues to Katie's whereabouts.

67
00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.880
Or a booby-trap.

68
00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:08.840
We have less than 52 hours
before they execute Katie.

69
00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:11.880
If we delay - Hugh. count yourself
lucky the Sword of Islam

70
00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.960
haven't already posted pictures of
dead soldiers on their website.

71
00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.120
Authorisation denied.

72
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:36.400
We've lost five men in 25 hours.

73
00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:40.320
What did you expect? Sir. Porter has
given us this location.

74
00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:44.600
We can't let these men's deaths be
in vain. I've no intention of that.

75
00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:49.440
You find me another mission as
cover... and you've got Charlie team.

76
00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.400
Sir.

77
00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.160
Hi. Alexandra.

78
00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.320
Is your mother here?

79
00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.800
Mum!

80
00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.200
This is about my dad. isn't it?

81
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.520
Hugh.
Diane.

82
00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:38.080
GCHQ monitoring recorded John
has a lost signal.

83
00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.680
Please speak English.
Alex.

84
00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:45.800
Your father volunteered for a
dangerous mission in Iraq.

85
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.800
Who sent him?
You know I can't tell you that.

86
00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:53.760
You. You sent him. didn't you?

87
00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:57.480
I can't go into detail but the
manner in which we lost contact

88
00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.920
with John makes us feel that -
Don't you dare! Don't you dare!

89
00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.240
My dad's not..

90
00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.360
I'm so sorry.
No. get off me!

91
00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.760
You're a liar!
Alex...

92
00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.560
Listen. um...

93
00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:22.440
..I know how much you've done
for John. Thank you.

94
00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:25.920
But... the truth is. Er...

95
00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.600
..we're all better off without him.

96
00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.520
Diane. he was -
No. you're better off too.

97
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.560
Whatever it was that made you
look out for him...

98
00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.480
..it's gone. You're free.

99
00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.000
Who are you?
Katie...

100
00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:13.240
My name's John.

101
00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.080
I'm SAS.

102
00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:23.120
It's alright. don't be frightened.

103
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.400
Katie...

104
00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.640
..we're gonna get you out of here.

105
00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.080
OK?

106
00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:37.400
You're a brave girl.
 Brave girl.

107
00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.320
Brave girl.

108
00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:43.440
Shh. It's OK.

109
00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.520
It's OK.

110
00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.960
Shh.

111
00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:07.880
Katie. look at me. Look at me.
Whatever happens. trust me!

112
00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:10.040
You trust me!

113
00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.560
You said you were here to negotiate.

114
00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:43.640
Is that true? Sorry. sir.
I can't answer that question.

115
00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:49.400
What is your mission? I'm sorry.
sir. I can't answer that question.

116
00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:17.800
By what means do the British plan
to rescue the hostage?

117
00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:21.080
I'm sorry. sir.
I can't answer that question.

118
00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:36.000
No! No! No. no!

119
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:37.960
What are you doing?! No!

120
00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:50.720
Tell me.

121
00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.960
Let me talk to her! If she wants me
to talk. she can tell me.

122
00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.400
Katie. Katie. look at me.

123
00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.360
Look at me.

124
00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.560
Trust me.

125
00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:21.680
Just so you know. I'm gonna kill
every single of of these bastards.

126
00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:26.160
Tell me! I'm sorry. sir.
I can't answer that question.

127
00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.640
Tell me!

128
00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:32.000
I'm sorry. sir. I can't answer
that question.

129
00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.080
Leave her alone. you fucker!

130
00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:50.360
Leave her alone!

131
00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.400
You let her suffer... to resist me.

132
00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:28.800
You're not gonna kill her. Not while
you still have her to bargain with.

133
00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:36.040
Katie Dartmouth's death was
inevitable the moment I took her.

134
00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:41.480
But because of you. I'm forced to

135
00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:44.880
bring forward the deadline
for her execution.

136
00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.720
We will kill her tomorrow at dawn.

137
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:56.920
And you will be first.

138
00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:43.180
"Charlie Team have been
deployed undercover

139
00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:46.580
of a joint operation
with our American friends."

140
00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:49.820
"How quickly can you be
where we lost Porter's signal?"

141
00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.820
We can be airborne immediately.
Good work.

142
00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:23.020
Shh. It's OK. It's OK.
It's only me. It's John.

143
00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:40.940
We're gonna get through this.
You and me.

144
00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:45.060
You know that. don't you?

145
00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:48.260
Yes.

146
00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:50.780
Good girl.

147
00:22:50.780 --> 00:22:54.700
I'm just gonna loosen these ropes
to make you more comfortable.

148
00:22:58.020 --> 00:23:00.300
Is that better?
Yeah.

149
00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:04.020
How does that arm feel?

150
00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:06.060
Just numb.

151
00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:12.500
I need to have a look at it.
Is that OK?

152
00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:16.860
Yeah. OK.

153
00:23:43.260 --> 00:23:45.340
Clear!

154
00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:50.100
'Clear!'

155
00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:55.740
'Clear!'

156
00:24:00.180 --> 00:24:05.340
How did you find me? The photo
you took of the young man...

157
00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:09.460
..led me to you.

158
00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:14.300
Really. I just wanted an autograph.

159
00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:20.580
Looks good.

160
00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:23.020
There's no infection.

161
00:24:24.660 --> 00:24:28.020
Now listen.

162
00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:30.660
They'll come for me first.

163
00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:35.540
That's our chance. I'll overpower
them. Then I'll come back for you.

164
00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:40.260
Gonna get you home. Katie.

165
00:24:44.780 --> 00:24:48.620
I'll need to put this hood back on.
I'm sorry.

166
00:24:48.620 --> 00:24:50.820
I understand.

167
00:24:57.020 --> 00:24:58.980
OK.

168
00:25:04.420 --> 00:25:07.220
OK.
Oh. please don't go.

169
00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:11.220
I'm not going anywhere.
I'm right here. I'm right here.

170
00:25:11.220 --> 00:25:15.860
OK. OK.

171
00:25:31.220 --> 00:25:34.340
'I think Porter
might still be alive.'

172
00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:37.820
'They've cleaned out. left the body
of one of their soldiers.'

173
00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:40.180
My guess is he's the man
who led Porter to them.

174
00:25:40.180 --> 00:25:43.620
If they left his body. Porter's
would be there. It stands to reason.

175
00:25:43.620 --> 00:25:48.060
There's a chance he's alive. We can
effect a rescue. Sir. One moment.

176
00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:52.700
All Islam locations are within
30 kilometres of each other.

177
00:25:52.700 --> 00:25:56.260
If we centre a radius
from the point of abduction.

178
00:25:56.260 --> 00:26:00.580
we narrow the search to specific
sites. Know the car he was driving?

179
00:26:00.580 --> 00:26:04.700
Yeah. a Range Rover. "Get back
to base but be airborne by dawn."

180
00:26:04.700 --> 00:26:08.340
We'll give you new coordinates
for an aerial search.

181
00:26:08.340 --> 00:26:11.780
You've got 25 hours. Layla.
There's still time.

182
00:26:30.180 --> 00:26:33.580
"This is Alpha.
Resuming search. Over."

183
00:26:47.100 --> 00:26:50.140
Don't move.

184
00:26:52.140 --> 00:26:54.700
What? What are we...?

185
00:26:54.700 --> 00:26:58.260
Where are you taking me? John!
John. where are they taking me?

186
00:26:58.260 --> 00:27:03.340
Oh. God! No!
Don't be frightened! Trust me.

187
00:27:03.340 --> 00:27:06.740
Help me! You bastard!
You said you'd take me first!

188
00:27:09.060 --> 00:27:11.220
I lied.

189
00:27:31.060 --> 00:27:33.580
Just coming up now. sir.

190
00:27:38.820 --> 00:27:43.540
Our demand for the release
of our brother has gone unheeded.

191
00:27:43.540 --> 00:27:47.980
They have shown no intention
of negotiating in good faith.

192
00:27:47.980 --> 00:27:52.140
That is why we shall execute Katie
Dartmouth in a few short minutes.

193
00:27:52.140 --> 00:27:56.980
Layla. they've brought it forward.
They'll execute Katie this morning.

194
00:28:21.940 --> 00:28:24.220
No! No!

195
00:28:24.220 --> 00:28:26.700
No! Don't!

196
00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:37.980
No! No! No!

197
00:28:37.980 --> 00:28:40.940
No! No!

198
00:28:53.300 --> 00:28:56.260
Oh. God! No!

199
00:29:06.620 --> 00:29:09.100
Katie!

200
00:30:42.260 --> 00:30:45.780
Don't shoot him. Don't. You know
why I have to kill you. don't you?

201
00:30:45.780 --> 00:30:48.700
Please!
I wanna hear you say it!

202
00:30:50.700 --> 00:30:53.900
John. think.
He could have shot you.

203
00:30:53.900 --> 00:30:56.460
This is for killing
Mike and Keith and for Steve.

204
00:31:01.460 --> 00:31:04.380
He says it wasn't him.
He says it wasn't him.

205
00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:08.220
No shit. He's got a gun in his face!
Does he look like a killer?

206
00:31:12.700 --> 00:31:16.180
He swears he didn't kill your
friends. Who did? Tell me that.

207
00:31:23.740 --> 00:31:26.220
We have to go now.
Move!

208
00:31:27.580 --> 00:31:31.420
Go! Move! Move!

209
00:31:37.260 --> 00:31:38.940
Go.

210
00:31:58.700 --> 00:32:00.700
"Heading north."

211
00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:04.740
"Continuing towards the radius."

212
00:32:04.740 --> 00:32:07.740
"Any developments?" They haven't
uploaded the execution.

213
00:32:07.740 --> 00:32:11.020
Until we hear otherwise.
assume Katie and Porter are alive.

214
00:32:14.100 --> 00:32:15.180
Hold on!

215
00:32:37.200 --> 00:32:40.400
John.
Yep.

216
00:32:47.540 --> 00:32:51.660
Give me a shout
if you see a phone box. Telephone?

217
00:32:55.220 --> 00:32:57.460
John.

218
00:32:57.460 --> 00:32:59.620
Fuck.

219
00:33:08.260 --> 00:33:10.580
Come on. pick up.

220
00:33:12.540 --> 00:33:16.900
"This is Lieutenant Thompson. Please
leave a message." Shit. Redial. OK.

221
00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:20.780
Hold on!

222
00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:25.660
We need to get off this road.

223
00:33:57.460 --> 00:34:00.100
Hello?
Hello? John!

224
00:34:00.100 --> 00:34:02.780
Layla? Layla. it's Porter.

225
00:34:02.780 --> 00:34:07.340
Porter. thank God! Sir.
we have contact from Bravo Team.

226
00:34:08.260 --> 00:34:10.740
Hold on. Layla.

227
00:34:11.940 --> 00:34:14.340
Right. get out.
get down behind the wheels.

228
00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:19.180
We have to make a stand. I have the
hostage. We now have the hostage.

229
00:34:20.340 --> 00:34:23.820
Bravo has Dartmouth. sir.
She's alive.

230
00:34:23.820 --> 00:34:27.820
What's your position?
Repeat. what's your position. Bravo?

231
00:34:27.820 --> 00:34:31.740
Just turned off a desert highway
heading southwest

232
00:34:31.740 --> 00:34:35.220
at an intersection of high voltage
pylons running north-south.

233
00:34:35.220 --> 00:34:37.700
Two vehicles in pursuit.

234
00:34:42.020 --> 00:34:46.740
"Found you. On our way. ETA
four minutes. Repeat. four minutes."

235
00:34:50.340 --> 00:34:51.980
Fuck.

236
00:34:53.500 --> 00:34:58.260
Pass me that. I also have Scarface.
Repeat. I also... Layla?

237
00:34:58.260 --> 00:35:00.900
"Porter?"
Layla!

238
00:35:00.900 --> 00:35:03.460
"Porter. can you hear me?"

239
00:35:10.140 --> 00:35:12.580
Shit.
"We have a visual on the pylons."

240
00:35:12.580 --> 00:35:16.220
"15km from target.
ETA three minutes."

241
00:35:25.100 --> 00:35:26.580
Fuck.

242
00:35:27.820 --> 00:35:29.900
Shit.

243
00:35:29.900 --> 00:35:32.340
I'm sorry.
Don't be.

244
00:35:53.580 --> 00:35:57.700
No! Hold position!

245
00:35:57.700 --> 00:36:00.660
There's someone else with Bravo.
sir!

246
00:36:00.660 --> 00:36:02.740
It's Scarface. sir!

247
00:36:02.740 --> 00:36:04.940
"I'll put you on head-cam."

248
00:36:08.980 --> 00:36:14.580
"Confirm. Bravo has the SOI soldier.
designation Scarface!"

249
00:36:14.580 --> 00:36:17.180
"Do we extract new contact?"

250
00:36:26.500 --> 00:36:29.140
"Do you copy?"

251
00:36:29.140 --> 00:36:33.220
"Do we extract new contact
with Bravo and hostage?"

252
00:36:33.220 --> 00:36:35.740
Extraction denied.

253
00:36:35.740 --> 00:36:38.860
Repeat. do not extract Scarface.

254
00:36:44.700 --> 00:36:47.740
Copy.
"Landing now."

255
00:36:59.260 --> 00:37:01.260
Stay low.

256
00:37:03.420 --> 00:37:06.180
Head down!

257
00:37:06.180 --> 00:37:09.700
Not you! On your knees!

258
00:37:11.020 --> 00:37:13.180
Katie. sit here.

259
00:37:16.540 --> 00:37:20.420
"This is 28 Alpha.
Hostage secure. Moving now."

260
00:37:20.420 --> 00:37:24.780
What? What are you doing?
Wait! As'ad!

261
00:37:26.180 --> 00:37:28.460
John. they're leaving him!

262
00:37:32.180 --> 00:37:35.500
Layla. we need to go back now!
Orders from Collinson!

263
00:37:35.500 --> 00:37:38.140
They'll kill him!

264
00:37:41.100 --> 00:37:44.620
No! Collinson. we need to go back!
Now!

265
00:37:44.620 --> 00:37:46.780
"Collinson. just give the order!"

266
00:37:46.780 --> 00:37:49.620
"Zero. this is 28 Alpha.
Do we return?"

267
00:37:49.620 --> 00:37:52.340
"Repeat. do we return? Over."

268
00:37:53.660 --> 00:37:56.180
"Collinson. don't do this!"

269
00:37:58.060 --> 00:38:02.460
"Collinson. you bastard! Collinson!
Collinson!"

270
00:38:50.060 --> 00:38:53.180
"The abducted television journalist
Katie Dartmouth

271
00:38:53.180 --> 00:38:57.780
is recovering in a US air base after
a daring rescue..."

272
00:38:57.780 --> 00:39:00.800
"Although no details have been
released by the Ministry of Defence.

273
00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:03.880
sources have told us that
the rescue came moments before

274
00:39:03.880 --> 00:39:06.640
the deadline was announced
for her execution."

275
00:39:06.640 --> 00:39:10.080
"Miss Dartmouth is expected
to fly home tomorrow morning."

276
00:39:10.080 --> 00:39:12.720
"We have this report..."
Oh. my God!

277
00:39:14.880 --> 00:39:19.000
Dad! Dad!

278
00:39:43.080 --> 00:39:46.200
Yeah?

279
00:39:53.680 --> 00:39:55.240
John.

280
00:39:59.480 --> 00:40:01.960
That's very kind.

281
00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:19.800
I'm one of the lucky ones.
I came home.

282
00:40:22.800 --> 00:40:26.840
My father supported the invasion
and the war that followed.

283
00:40:26.840 --> 00:40:30.200
an extension of which
is still going on in Afghanistan.

284
00:40:32.880 --> 00:40:35.600
My family have had a taste
of what British forces

285
00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:39.280
and Iraqi families have gone through
these past few years.

286
00:40:39.280 --> 00:40:41.840
And we are humbled by it.

287
00:40:45.760 --> 00:40:49.720
My heart goes out to those families
on both sides

288
00:40:49.720 --> 00:40:52.440
whose loved ones
will never come home.

289
00:41:09.080 --> 00:41:11.360
I owe you an apology.

290
00:41:12.600 --> 00:41:14.280
Oh?

291
00:41:16.680 --> 00:41:19.040
You did an extraordinary thing
out there.

292
00:41:22.200 --> 00:41:25.240
Not gonna kiss me. are you?
No.

293
00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:29.800
Don't get all sentimental on me
like that.

294
00:41:29.800 --> 00:41:32.240
I think I preferred you
with low self-esteem.

295
00:41:36.480 --> 00:41:38.960
What will you do now?

296
00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:42.720
I'm gonna see a man about a job.

297
00:41:46.240 --> 00:41:48.600
I'm glad you came in.

298
00:41:48.600 --> 00:41:53.040
As a friend. I owe you
an explanation about Scarface.

299
00:41:54.960 --> 00:41:57.720
As'ad.
Yes.

300
00:41:58.760 --> 00:42:00.800
As'ad.

301
00:42:01.880 --> 00:42:04.400
I was forced to weigh
the intelligence value

302
00:42:04.400 --> 00:42:07.480
he might have been able to provide
against the risk he posed

303
00:42:07.480 --> 00:42:11.680
as a known terrorist.
Suppose he'd had a change of heart

304
00:42:11.680 --> 00:42:14.000
and tried to bring down
the helicopter?

305
00:42:14.000 --> 00:42:17.960
We could've lost Katie on the very
brink of getting her to safety.

306
00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:22.600
Katie.... I need you to tell me

307
00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:25.360
everything As'ad said to you.

308
00:42:28.680 --> 00:42:32.240
About what happened
the night you saved his life? Yeah.

309
00:42:36.200 --> 00:42:37.960
He said...

310
00:42:40.240 --> 00:42:44.200
He said that the man who killed
your friends was another soldier.

311
00:42:45.640 --> 00:42:47.760
An Iraqi soldier...

312
00:42:52.360 --> 00:42:54.720
..or a British soldier?

313
00:42:58.560 --> 00:43:00.800
You do understand. don't you. John?

314
00:43:02.320 --> 00:43:04.480
Of course.

315
00:43:04.480 --> 00:43:08.160
I would've done exactly the same
thing if I was in your shoes.

316
00:43:08.160 --> 00:43:10.120
Good.

317
00:43:11.280 --> 00:43:12.920
Good.

318
00:43:14.400 --> 00:43:17.120
So. have you come to a decision?

319
00:43:20.320 --> 00:43:22.960
About our offer to join Section 20?

320
00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:26.040
Yeah.

321
00:43:28.280 --> 00:43:30.520
Yes. I have.
